Subject: [PATCH] metal0 host-owner enrollment: loopback MetaMask handoff
 (source only, inactive)

Two administrator stages on the reviewed transport (handoff-server.mjs unchanged, sha256 fb189e46):
optional fixed 0.000005 ETH transfer to the existing metal0 operator, then acceptOwner(metal0) with
zero ETH only once the operator's proposal of exactly the administrator is two blocks deep. Frozen
target/calldata/value; fresh two-provider state, simulation, estimate and fee checks per preparation;
state-based refusals against early, duplicate and lost-response transactions; exact receipt and
post-state verification. Read-only preflight for root. Book activation excluded. Nothing was served,
signed, sent or funded; no live preflight has been run.

Tests (fake two-provider Base, loopback only, via claude-test-queue.py):
- test/stages.test.mjs 11/11 at 256 MiB (peak 222 MiB, logs/stages-5)
- test/browser.test.mjs 3/3 at 512 MiB, headless Chromium + fake EIP-6963 MetaMask (peak 429 MiB, logs/browser-4)
- gitleaks on the staged diff: no leaks (logs/gitleaks-1)
